<h2>Our service area in Hays County and Central Texas</h2>
<p>San Marcos is the county seat of Hays County, on Interstate 35 (I-35) between Austin and San Antonio. Its weather risks are real. NOAA storm records for Hays County show hail peaking in April and May, and on May 9, 2024, hail up to 3 inches and wind gusts near 70 mph damaged roofs and downed trees in and around San Marcos. The area also sits in Flash Flood Alley along the Balcones Escarpment: during the Memorial Day flood of May 2015, the San Marcos River near San Marcos crested at 43.08 feet. Winter Storm Uri in February 2021 left many homes with burst pipes. Our <a href="/storm-history/">San Marcos storm history</a> page covers more of that record.</p>
